    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two serums built around vitamin C\n\n[Lelive All Glow'd Up Brighten + Clarify Serum](/reviews/lelive-all-glowd-up-serum) and [The Ordinary Ascorbic Acid + Alpha Arbutin](/reviews/ordinary-vitc-alpha-arbutin) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on vitamin C, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 4.1× the other (R199 for The Ordinary, R814 for Lelive). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | Lelive All Glow'd Up Brighten + Clarify Serum | The Ordinary Ascorbic Acid + Alpha Arbutin |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Vitamin C Derivative, Botanical Brighteners | Ascorbic Acid, Alpha Arbutin |\n| Indicative price | R814 | R199 |\n| Suits | Dull, Uneven | Dull, Uneven |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 7.3/10 | 7.5/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list vitamin C-related ingredients among their key actives (Vitamin C Derivative, Botanical Brighteners for Lelive; Ascorbic Acid, Alpha Arbutin for The Ordinary), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | Lelive | The Ordinary |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 7.0 | 7.0 |\n| Value | 6.5 | 8.5 |\n| Texture | 7.5 | 6.5 |\n| SA climate fit | 8.0 | 8.0 |\n\nOn efficacy they're effectively level (7.0 vs 7.0). The Ordinary scores higher on value (8.5 vs 6.5). Lelive scores higher on texture (7.5 vs 6.5). On SA climate fit they're effectively level (8.0 vs 8.0). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list dull and uneven skin as a match. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: Lelive — A competent brightening serum, though premium USD-linked pricing makes it a harder sell than local alternatives at a third of the cost. The Ordinary — An affordable antioxidant and brightening combination for AM use across all SA climate zones.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nThe Ordinary is the cheaper option at R199; Lelive sits at R814. Prices are indicative and change often. Lelive is listed at Brand Direct, and The Ordinary at Clicks, Dis-Chem. The Ordinary also scores at least as well on value (8.5 vs 6.5), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick Lelive if texture matters most to you; pick The Ordinary if value does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
