    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two serums built around brightening actives\n\n[Fundamentals 2% Alpha Arbutin + 2% Licorice Serum](/reviews/fundamentals-arbutin-licorice) and [Yearn Skin Hyperpigmentation Correcting Serum](/reviews/ys-hyperpigmentation-serum) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on brightening actives, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 2.0× the other (R149 for Fundamentals, R300 for Yearn Skin). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | Fundamentals 2% Alpha Arbutin + 2% Licorice Serum | Yearn Skin Hyperpigmentation Correcting Serum |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Alpha Arbutin 2%, Licorice Root Extract | Alpha Arbutin, Tranexamic Acid |\n| Indicative price | R149 | R300 |\n| Suits | All, Dark Marks | Dark Marks, All |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 8.3/10 | 7.6/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list brightening actives-related ingredients among their key actives (Alpha Arbutin 2%, Licorice Root Extract for Fundamentals; Alpha Arbutin, Tranexamic Acid for Yearn Skin), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | Fundamentals | Yearn Skin |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 7.5 | 7.5 |\n| Value | 9.5 | 7.5 |\n| Texture | 8.0 | 7.5 |\n| SA climate fit | 8.0 | 8.0 |\n\nOn efficacy they're effectively level (7.5 vs 7.5). Fundamentals scores higher on value (9.5 vs 7.5). Fundamentals scores higher on texture (8.0 vs 7.5). On SA climate fit they're effectively level (8.0 vs 8.0). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list all and dark marks skin as a match. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: Fundamentals — Arbutin plus licorice (glabridin) give dual tyrosinase inhibition for excellent-value pigment correction — one of the best brightening buys in SA. Yearn Skin — A reasonable tyrosinase-inhibiting approach to tone correction from a brand with a tight, sensible focus rather than a scattershot general range — pair with daily SPF.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nFundamentals is the cheaper option at R149; Yearn Skin sits at R300. Prices are indicative and change often. Fundamentals is listed at Brand Direct, Clicks, and Yearn Skin at Brand Direct. Fundamentals also scores at least as well on value (9.5 vs 7.5), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick Fundamentals if value and texture matters most to you; pick Yearn Skin if price and simplicity does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
