    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two serums built around brightening actives\n\n[Fundamentals 2% Alpha Arbutin + 2% Licorice Serum](/reviews/fundamentals-arbutin-licorice) and [Black African Organics Melanin-Rich Skin Brightening Serum](/reviews/bao-melanin-brightening-serum) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on brightening actives, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 1.8× the other (R149 for Fundamentals, R265 for Black African Organics). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | Fundamentals 2% Alpha Arbutin + 2% Licorice Serum | Black African Organics Melanin-Rich Skin Brightening Serum |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Alpha Arbutin 2%, Licorice Root Extract | Alpha Arbutin, Niacinamide |\n| Indicative price | R149 | R265 |\n| Suits | All, Dark Marks | Dark Marks, All |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 8.3/10 | 7.5/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list brightening actives-related ingredients among their key actives (Alpha Arbutin 2%, Licorice Root Extract for Fundamentals; Alpha Arbutin, Niacinamide for Black African Organics), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | Fundamentals | Black African Organics |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 7.5 | 7.0 |\n| Value | 9.5 | 7.5 |\n| Texture | 8.0 | 7.5 |\n| SA climate fit | 8.0 | 8.0 |\n\nFundamentals scores higher on efficacy (7.5 vs 7.0). Fundamentals scores higher on value (9.5 vs 7.5). Fundamentals scores higher on texture (8.0 vs 7.5). On SA climate fit they're effectively level (8.0 vs 8.0). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list all and dark marks skin as a match. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: Fundamentals — Arbutin plus licorice (glabridin) give dual tyrosinase inhibition for excellent-value pigment correction — one of the best brightening buys in SA. Black African Organics — A sound tyrosinase-inhibiting approach to the post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation that generic 'brightening' marketing often glosses over on deeper skin tones.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nFundamentals is the cheaper option at R149; Black African Organics sits at R265. Prices are indicative and change often. Fundamentals is listed at Brand Direct, Clicks, and Black African Organics at Brand Direct. Fundamentals also scores at least as well on value (9.5 vs 7.5), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick Fundamentals if efficacy and value and texture matters most to you; pick Black African Organics if price and simplicity does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
