    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two moisturisers built around hyaluronic acid\n\n[The Ordinary Natural Moisturizing Factors + HA](/reviews/ordinary-nmf-ha) and [Avon Anew Hydra Fusion Deep Moisture Cream](/reviews/avon-anew-hydra-fusion-cream) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on hyaluronic acid, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 1.7× the other (R149 for The Ordinary, R259 for Avon). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | The Ordinary Natural Moisturizing Factors + HA | Avon Anew Hydra Fusion Deep Moisture Cream |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Natural Moisturizing Factors, Hyaluronic Acid | Hyaluronic Acid, Glycerin |\n| Indicative price | R149 | R259 |\n| Suits | Normal, Dry | Dry, Dehydrated, Normal |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 7.8/10 | 7.1/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list hyaluronic acid-related ingredients among their key actives (Natural Moisturizing Factors, Hyaluronic Acid for The Ordinary; Hyaluronic Acid, Glycerin for Avon), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | The Ordinary | Avon |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 6.5 | 6.5 |\n| Value | 9.0 | 7.5 |\n| Texture | 7.5 | 7.5 |\n| SA climate fit | 8.0 | 7.0 |\n\nOn efficacy they're effectively level (6.5 vs 6.5). The Ordinary scores higher on value (9.0 vs 7.5). On texture they're effectively level (7.5 vs 7.5). The Ordinary scores higher on SA climate fit (8.0 vs 7.0). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list normal and dry skin as a match. Avon additionally lists dehydrated skin. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: The Ordinary — A barrier-support moisturiser that's light enough for KZN humidity but layers well on the Highveld too. Avon — A dependable, hyaluronic-acid-led daily moisturiser that pairs sensibly with the Anew vitamin C serum in an AM/PM routine — nothing showy, just a solid hydration layer at a direct-sales price.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nThe Ordinary is the cheaper option at R149; Avon sits at R259. Prices are indicative and change often. The Ordinary is listed at Clicks, Dis-Chem, and Avon at Brand Direct. The Ordinary also scores at least as well on value (9.0 vs 7.5), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick The Ordinary if value and SA climate fit matters most to you; pick Avon if price and simplicity does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
