    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two moisturisers built around hyaluronic acid\n\n[Standard Beauty Moisture Bomb Daily Moisturiser](/reviews/sb-moisture-bomb) and [Sorbet Skin Hydrating Day Cream](/reviews/ss-hydrating-day-cream) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on hyaluronic acid, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 1.5× the other (R195 for Standard Beauty, R299 for Sorbet Skin). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | Standard Beauty Moisture Bomb Daily Moisturiser | Sorbet Skin Hydrating Day Cream |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Glycerin, Hyaluronic Acid | Glycerin, Hyaluronic Acid |\n| Indicative price | R195 | R299 |\n| Suits | Normal, Combination, Dehydrated | Normal, Combination |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 8.0/10 | 7.0/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list hyaluronic acid-related ingredients among their key actives (Glycerin, Hyaluronic Acid for Standard Beauty; Glycerin, Hyaluronic Acid for Sorbet Skin), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | Standard Beauty | Sorbet Skin |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 7.0 | 6.0 |\n| Value | 8.0 | 7.0 |\n| Texture | 8.5 | 7.5 |\n| SA climate fit | 8.5 | 7.5 |\n\nStandard Beauty scores higher on efficacy (7.0 vs 6.0). Standard Beauty scores higher on value (8.0 vs 7.0). Standard Beauty scores higher on texture (8.5 vs 7.5). Standard Beauty scores higher on SA climate fit (8.5 vs 7.5). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list normal and combination skin as a match. Standard Beauty additionally lists dehydrated skin. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: Standard Beauty — A humectant-forward daily gel-cream that layers easily under SPF and works across most SA climate zones. Sorbet Skin — An easy, dependable daily moisturiser — nothing here beats the more specialised actives brands in this file on efficacy, but it's a fine everyday layer.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nStandard Beauty is the cheaper option at R195; Sorbet Skin sits at R299. Prices are indicative and change often. Standard Beauty is listed at Brand Direct, Takealot, and Sorbet Skin at Clicks, Brand Direct. Standard Beauty also scores at least as well on value (8.0 vs 7.0), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick Standard Beauty if efficacy and value and texture and SA climate fit matters most to you; pick Sorbet Skin if price and simplicity does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
