    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two moisturisers built around ceramides\n\n[Standard Beauty CERious PrOATection Moisturiser](/reviews/sb-cerious-proatection) and [Future Me Barrier Repair Moisturiser](/reviews/fm-barrier-repair-moisturiser) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on ceramides, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 1.4× the other (R195 for Standard Beauty, R265 for Future Me). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | Standard Beauty CERious PrOATection Moisturiser | Future Me Barrier Repair Moisturiser |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Ceramide NP, Panthenol, Hemi-Squalane, CoQ10 | Ceramides, Peptides |\n| Indicative price | R195 | R265 |\n| Suits | Dry, Sensitive, Combination, Mature | Dry, Sensitive, All |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 8.8/10 | 7.5/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list ceramides-related ingredients among their key actives (Ceramide NP, Panthenol, Hemi-Squalane, CoQ10 for Standard Beauty; Ceramides, Peptides for Future Me), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | Standard Beauty | Future Me |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 8.5 | 7.0 |\n| Value | 9.5 | 7.5 |\n| Texture | 8.5 | 8.0 |\n| SA climate fit | 8.5 | 7.5 |\n\nStandard Beauty scores higher on efficacy (8.5 vs 7.0). Standard Beauty scores higher on value (9.5 vs 7.5). Standard Beauty scores higher on texture (8.5 vs 8.0). Standard Beauty scores higher on SA climate fit (8.5 vs 7.5). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list dry and sensitive skin as a match. Standard Beauty additionally lists combination and mature skin. Future Me additionally lists all skin. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: Standard Beauty — A ceramide, panthenol and squalane barrier cream that genuinely earns its price — one of the best-value moisturisers we've tested locally. Future Me — A ceramide-forward barrier cream that layers well — a modern take on a classic actives-plus-barrier routine.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nStandard Beauty is the cheaper option at R195; Future Me sits at R265. Prices are indicative and change often. Standard Beauty is listed at Brand Direct, Takealot, Superbalist, and Future Me at Brand Direct. Standard Beauty also scores at least as well on value (9.5 vs 7.5), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick Standard Beauty if efficacy and value and texture and SA climate fit matters most to you; pick Future Me if price and simplicity does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
