    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two serums built around hyaluronic acid\n\n[Standard Beauty Hyaluronic Acid + Reneseed Peptides Serum](/reviews/sb-ha-reneseed-peptides) and [Skin Functional 3.5% Hyaluronic Acid + Peptides + NMF](/reviews/sf-ha-peptides-nmf) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on hyaluronic acid, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 1.2× the other (R190 for Skin Functional, R229 for Standard Beauty). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | Standard Beauty Hyaluronic Acid + Reneseed Peptides Serum | Skin Functional 3.5% Hyaluronic Acid + Peptides + NMF |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Hyaluronic Acid, Peptides | Hyaluronic Acid, NMF Complex |\n| Indicative price | R229 | R190 |\n| Suits | All, Dehydrated | All, Dehydrated |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 7.6/10 | 7.9/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list hyaluronic acid-related ingredients among their key actives (Hyaluronic Acid, Peptides for Standard Beauty; Hyaluronic Acid, NMF Complex for Skin Functional), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | Standard Beauty | Skin Functional |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 7.0 | 7.5 |\n| Value | 7.5 | 8.0 |\n| Texture | 8.5 | 8.5 |\n| SA climate fit | 7.5 | 7.5 |\n\nSkin Functional scores higher on efficacy (7.5 vs 7.0). Skin Functional scores higher on value (8.0 vs 7.5). On texture they're effectively level (8.5 vs 8.5). On SA climate fit they're effectively level (7.5 vs 7.5). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list all and dehydrated skin as a match. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: Standard Beauty — Multi-weight HA plus peptides makes a genuinely good hydrator — pair with an occlusive on the dry Highveld to stop it drawing water from the skin. Skin Functional — A layered HA and NMF hydrator that plumps well — seal with an occlusive if you're on the dry Highveld.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nSkin Functional is the cheaper option at R190; Standard Beauty sits at R229. Prices are indicative and change often. Standard Beauty is listed at Brand Direct, Takealot, and Skin Functional at Dis-Chem, SkinMiles. Skin Functional also scores at least as well on value (8.0 vs 7.5), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick Standard Beauty if price and simplicity matters most to you; pick Skin Functional if efficacy and value does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
