    "bodyMarkdown": "## Two serums built around niacinamide\n\n[Skoon B3 Barrier Repair NanoPillow Serum](/reviews/skoon-b3-barrier-nanopillow) and [Fundamentals 6% Niacinamide Serum](/reviews/fundamentals-niacinamide-6) are the kind of pair a South African shopper really does weigh up: both lean on niacinamide, they suit overlapping skin types, and one costs about 5.4× the other (R129 for Fundamentals, R700 for Skoon). That price gap is the question this showdown answers: what you get, and don't get, for the extra money.\n\n## What's in each\n\n| | Skoon B3 Barrier Repair NanoPillow Serum | Fundamentals 6% Niacinamide Serum |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key ingredients | Niacinamide, Electrospun Nanofibre | Niacinamide 6%, Hyaluronic Acid Crosspolymer, Panthenol |\n| Indicative price | R700 | R129 |\n| Suits | Sensitive, Compromised, All | Oily, Combination, Sensitive, Acne-prone |\n| SkinLabs overall score | 7.4/10 | 8.4/10 |\n\nBoth formulas list niacinamide-related ingredients among their key actives (Niacinamide, Electrospun Nanofibre for Skoon; Niacinamide 6%, Hyaluronic Acid Crosspolymer, Panthenol for Fundamentals), so the real differences come from the rest of each formula and from how it behaves on skin.\n\n## How the SkinLabs scores compare\n\nWe score every product on four things, independently: efficacy, value, texture and fit for South African conditions. Here's how this pair lines up:\n\n| Score (out of 10) | Skoon | Fundamentals |\n|---|---|---|\n| Efficacy | 7.5 | 7.5 |\n| Value | 6.0 | 9.5 |\n| Texture | 8.0 | 8.0 |\n| SA climate fit | 8.0 | 8.5 |\n\nOn efficacy they're effectively level (7.5 vs 7.5). Fundamentals scores higher on value (9.5 vs 6.0). On texture they're effectively level (8.0 vs 8.0). Fundamentals scores higher on SA climate fit (8.5 vs 8.0). These scores reflect SkinLabs' editorial assessment of publicly available ingredient and pricing information, not laboratory or clinical testing.\n\n## Who each one suits\n\nBoth list sensitive skin as a match. Skoon additionally lists compromised and all skin. Fundamentals additionally lists oily, combination and acne-prone skin. Our verdicts, in each review's own words: Skoon — A novel waterless electrospun-nanofibre niacinamide delivery format — genuinely innovative, though the premium format pricing is a hard sell. Fundamentals — Honest, no-frills and superb value — 6% is a gentle, effective sweet spot, proving you rarely need to pay more than R250 for a single-active serum.\n\n## Price and where to buy\n\nFundamentals is the cheaper option at R129; Skoon sits at R700. Prices are indicative and change often. Skoon is listed at Brand Direct, Faithful to Nature, and Fundamentals at Brand Direct, Clicks, Superbalist. Fundamentals also scores at least as well on value (9.5 vs 6.0), so the cheaper product is not a compromise on that front.\n\n## Our take\n\nThere's no universal winner here. Pick Skoon if price and simplicity matters most to you; pick Fundamentals if value and SA climate fit does. Whichever you choose, patch-test a new product first, and remember this is cosmetic guidance, not medical advice.",
